# Introduction to Basic-Mechanical-Engineering

It introduces the core principles of mechanics, materials, thermodynamics, and manufacturing processes.
The subject helps students understand how machines and mechanical systems are designed, analyzed, and operated. By covering basic concepts such as force, motion, energy conversion, and material properties, the course prepares aspiring engineers to solve practical engineering problems and build a strong base for advanced mechanical engineering studies.

# Structure

- /Thermodynamics/
- /Zeroth law & First law of Thermodynamics/
- /Second law of thermodynamics/
- /Introduction to IC Engines/
- /Simple Stress & Strain/